{% doc %}
  blocks/card-content.liquid

  The panel that sits on a picture — the frosted card in the bottom corner of the
  *FAQ: Banner* image, holding a heading, a line of text and a button.

  ## A group, with one thing added

  Layout, width, border, radius, padding and the alignment swap are
  `snippets/group.liquid` — the same file `blocks/group.liquid`,
  `blocks/section-header.liquid` and `blocks/image-card.liquid` render through,
  so a merchant who has laid out any of them has laid this out too.

  What it adds is the surface a card on a photograph needs and a plain group
  does not:

      Background + Opacity   one colour and one slider rather than a colour
                             picker the merchant has to know accepts alpha
      Blur                   the frosted pane behind the text
      Text color             set here, because the panel's contrast comes from
                             the photograph rather than from a colour scheme

  ## Why the colour is two settings

  A translucent panel is a colour *and* how much of it there is, and merchants
  reach for a slider for the second one. The alpha is applied to the colour with
  `color_modify` rather than to the element with `opacity`, because `opacity`
  would fade the heading, the text and the button along with the pane behind
  them — the one thing the pane exists to keep readable.

  ## The blur needs something behind it to blur

  `backdrop-filter` samples what is painted underneath. On a card whose picture
  is the group's background that is the photograph, which is what this block is
  for and why it ships blurring. Dropped into a section with a flat background it
  blurs a flat colour and appears to do nothing — not a bug to guard against, but
  worth knowing before reaching for the slider and concluding it is broken.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  comment
    The alpha goes into the colour. `opacity` on the element would fade the
    content the panel is there to make readable.
  endcomment
  assign background_paint = ''
  if s.background_color != blank
    assign background_alpha = s.background_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    assign background_alpha = background_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | color_modify: 'alpha', background_alpha
  endif
-%}

{%- capture card_style -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    --group-background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.text_color != blank -%}
    color: {{ s.text_color }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture children -%}
  {% content_for 'blocks' %}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  `styles` rather than a `style` attribute of this block's own: the group snippet
  writes one already, and a tag with two of them keeps the first and loses the
  rest — the bug `snippets/spacing.liquid` documents at length.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'group',
   children: children,
   settings: s,
   extra_classes: 'card-content',
   styles: card_style,
   shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes %}

